All five modules are complete and mutually consistent. A quick trace of the key flows confirms correctness: `receive` checks qty > 0 → ref uniqueness → sku/location existence → capacity (summing all skus at dst) → mutates stock → appends exactly one movement; any failure before mutation leaves the store untouched, so a failed operation neither burns a timestamp nor consumes a ref (verified by `test_failed_op_does_not_burn_timestamps_or_refs`). The on-disk format matches the fixture exactly (plain dicts under the four keys), `load()` rehydrates them into dataclasses, and every write goes through temp-file + `os.replace`. Run everything with `python -m unittest tests` (18 tests pass), and drive the CLI via e.g. `python cli.py --db store.json transfer SKU-1 5 A B ref-9` or `python cli.py --db store.json report`.
